  "id": "treatment-withholding",
  "term": "treatment withholding",
  "definition": "Treatment withholding means not starting or stopping a specific treatment for a patient or, in research, for a study participant under the study plan. It can involve life-prolonging care but is broader than that, and it differs from refusal to treat, which focuses on a clinician or facility declining requested care.",
